{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01VFUh5UbLsNGwx9ioy17fS2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed predicted data for each planned experiment in the `experiment_plan` under the \"worst\" tier scenario. Let me identify the planned experiments:\n\n1. **diagnostic-rerepair** (status: planned) - the re-repair downstream proof-of-concept\n2. **swebench-pertest-data** (status: planned) - Docker re-evaluation for SWE-bench PerTest dataset\n\nAnd there's also the `what_if` experiment:\n- **re-repair-phase1-instruct** - the improved re-repair with fixed confounds\n\n\n- Plus the currently running experiments: **deepseek-cwm-repo**, **deepseek-cls-repo-s123**, **deepseek-cwm-repo-s123**, and **deepseek-cls-repo-v4**.\n\nFor the worst-case scenario, I'm defining this as re-repair showing flat or negative results that mirror phase0 outcomes, and DeepSeek repo results being confounded. The core hypothesis I'm testing is whether re-repair phase1 achieves a resolve rate improvement of less than 3 percentage points.\n\nNow I'm looking at the expected metric ranges across these experiments to understand what would constitute failure versus success.\n\nFor the planned experiments, diagnostic-rerepair maps to the re-repair phase, while swebench-pertest-data is just data construction so it's less vulnerable to worst-case outcomes. The running experiments on DeepSeek are where I expect the most confounding—CWM and CLS variants likely won't converge properly or will fall below the majority baseline, making it hard to draw meaningful conclusions about whether the approach actually helps.\n\nLet me work through the specific predictions for each experiment and what the worst-case results would look like.\n\nFor deepseek-cwm-repo, the unparseable rate could swing anywhere from 5% to 60%, but the worst narrative isn't necessarily the extreme—it's the middle ground where we get maybe 30-50% unparseable, enough to degrade performance but not so obvious that it clearly explains the gap. DeepSeek's tokenizer handles structured output better than Qwen's, so I'm not expecting the catastrophic 93% unparseable rate we saw there, but repo-level parsing is harder than function-level, so accuracy could still end up close to or below the majority baseline.\n\nLooking at deepseek-cls-repo, the accuracy range of 70-78% is actually concerning because the majority baseline sits around 73%—meaning CLS could underperform even the naive baseline, which undermines the whole premise that CLS is the reliable formulation. And the CLS-CWM gap of [-5, 5]pp is ambiguous enough that CWM might actually outperform CLS, directly contradicting what we saw with Qwen where CLS dominated by 19-26 percentage points.\n\nThe seed variance is also a major confound here. With only 48 test samples, the variance is enormous—the trajectory experiments already show a 15 percentage point spread across seeds, so any single result could be noise rather than signal.\n\nFor the re-repair-phase1-instruct results, the deltas are all essentially flat: CLS-diagnostic barely improves over the baseline, the oracle only marginally beats CLS, and random context performs just as well as CLS-specific diagnostics. This suggests the entire re-repair experiment fails to show that better diagnostics actually drive downstream improvements.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":33642,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":33642},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b649b12d-6842-4938-9e21-936da6c17cfc","uuid":"571994b9-8f2c-4213-86e5-3b83514bf207"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01VFUh5UbLsNGwx9ioy17fS2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: \"完全放弃 re-repair section，不放入论文。Reframe: (1) efficiency 6-9x speedup 作为核心 practical contribution; (2) 强化 error complementarity (oracle 90.63%) 作为 formulations are complementary 的证据; (3) DeepSeek repo scope down 为 case study 而非 systematic comparison。仍投 EMNLP Main，但 novelty argument 必须极其清晰。Fallback: ICSE 2027。\"\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"re-repair-phase1-instruct\"\n    plan_id: \"diagnostic-rerepair\"\n    description: \"Re-repair with Qwen3-8B-Instruct on 60 SWE-bench instances, 5 conditions (A1-minimal, A2-test-names, B-CLS-diagnostic, C-oracle, D-random), pass@1/pass@5, Docker eval, paired design.\"\n    expected_results:\n      n_instances: 60\n      n_conditions: 5\n      samples_per_condition: 5\n      A1_minimal_resolve_rate_pass1: 0.183\n      A2_test_names_resolve_rate_pass1: 0.200\n      B_cls_diagnostic_resolve_rate_pass1: 0.200\n      C_oracle_diagnostic_resolve_rate_pass1: 0.217\n      D_random_diagnostic_resolve_rate_pass1: 0.193\n      A1_resolve_rate_pass5: 0.317\n      B_resolve_rate_pass5: 0.333\n      C_resolve_rate_pass5: 0.367\n      D_resolve_rate_pass5: 0.317\n      delta_B_vs_A1_pp: 1.7\n      delta_C_vs_A1_pp: 3.4\n      delta_D_vs_A1_pp: 1.0\n      delta_B_vs_D_pp: 0.7\n      delta_C_vs_B_pp: 1.7\n      paired_mcnemar_B_vs_A1_p: 0.72\n      paired_mcnemar_B_vs_D_p: 0.83\n      CI_95_B_vs_A1: [-4.2, 7.5]\n      prompt_format1_delta_B_A1: 2.3\n      prompt_format2_delta_B_A1: 1.0\n    result_rationale: \"Repair agent (Qwen3-8B-Instruct) 本身 resolve rate ~18% — 在此低基线下 per-test diagnostic 的信息增益被 agent 的代码理解能力瓶颈淹没。Agent 在多数情况下无法利用 'test_X fails with expected Y got Z' 信息来定位 bug，因为 bug 本身需要 repo-level 理解。Oracle (C) 仅略好于 CLS (B) 证明即使 diagnostic 完美准确也帮助有限。Random (D) 与 B 无显著差异，说明 agent 对任何额外 context 的反应类似 — 可能只是 prompt 长度/结构的 placebo effect 而非 CLS-specific signal。60 instances × 5 samples 的 power 不足以检测 <5pp 的差异 (所需 n≈200+)。复现 phase0 的 null pattern: 所有带 diagnostic 的 condition 都与 control 无统计显著差异。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Re-repair Resolve Rate by Condition\"\n        columns: [\"Condition\", \"pass@1\", \"pass@5\", \"Δ vs A1 (pp)\", \"p-value\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"A1 (minimal)\", \"18.3%\", \"31.7%\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"A2 (test-names)\", \"20.0%\", \"30.0%\", \"+1.7\", \"0.81\"]\n          - [\"B (CLS-diag)\", \"20.0%\", \"33.3%\", \"+1.7\", \"0.72\"]\n          - [\"C (Oracle-diag)\", \"21.7%\", \"36.7%\", \"+3.4\", \"0.48\"]\n          - [\"D (Random-diag)\", \"19.3%\", \"31.7%\", \"+1.0\", \"0.89\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart showing resolve rate across 5 conditions with 95% CI error bars; all CIs heavily overlap, visually indistinguishable.\"\n    analysis: \"完全 null result。B vs A1 的 1.7pp 差异远在 noise 范围内 (CI: -4.2 to +7.5)。B vs D 差异 0.7pp 证明 CLS-specific information 没有比 random noise 更好。即使 oracle (C) 也仅 +3.4pp，表明 per-test failure localization 本身对当前 repair agent 无用。结论: diagnostic info 不改变 repair agent 行为。此 section 如放入论文只会暴露 'no downstream utility' 弱点，应完全删除。\"\n\n  - name: \"deepseek-cls-repo-v4\"\n    plan_id: \"repo-level-training\"\n    description: \"DeepSeek-R1-0528-Qwen3-8B LoRA classification at repo-level, seed 42, 8k seq length, same SWE-bench-PerTest data as Qwen experiments.\"\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 74.8\n      f1_macro: 65.2\n      f1_pass: 82.1\n      f1_fail: 48.3\n      precision_fail: 55.7\n      recall_fail: 42.8\n      precision_pass: 79.6\n      recall_pass: 84.7\n      majority_baseline: 72.96\n      gap_vs_majority_pp: 1.84\n      unparseable_pct: 1.8\n      train_loss_final: 0.42\n      eval_loss_best: 0.38\n      best_checkpoint: \"checkpoint-400\"\n      total_samples: 9784\n      overfitting_detected: true\n    result_rationale: \"DeepSeek 8B (distilled from R1) 在 repo-level 上表现远不如 function-level (func: 86.9%)。原因: (1) repo-level 输入平均 6-8k tokens，DeepSeek 的 LoRA rank=16 容量不足以学会长上下文中的 pass/fail 信号; (2) 训练数据仅 ~3k repo-level instances (vs func-level 9.5k)，data-starved; (3) 74.8% 仅高于 majority baseline 1.84pp，实质上模型主要学到了 class prior 而非 discriminative features。与 Qwen 8B 在同数据上的 84.79% (ckpt-400) 相比低 10pp，表明 DeepSeek distilled model 的 LoRA fine-tuning effectiveness 显著低于 Qwen — 这是 confound: 我们无法区分 'formulation difference' 和 'model fine-tuning efficiency difference'。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: DeepSeek Repo-level CLS Performance\"\n        columns: [\"Checkpoint\", \"Accuracy\", \"F1-macro\", \"Fail-F1\", \"Gap vs Majority\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"ckpt-200\", \"71.2%\", \"58.3\", \"38.7\", \"-1.76pp\"]\n          - [\"ckpt-400\", \"74.8%\", \"65.2\", \"48.3\", \"+1.84pp\"]\n          - [\"ckpt-600\", \"73.1%\", \"62.8\", \"44.1\", \"+0.14pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Learning curve showing rapid overfitting after step 400, eval loss climbing while train loss drops.\"\n    analysis: \"CLS 在 DeepSeek repo-level 仅比 majority baseline 高 ~2pp，远低于 Qwen 8B 的 +12pp gap。这使 cross-model comparison 失去意义: 如果 CLS 本身不 work，CLS vs CWM 的比较没有 informative value。Confound: DeepSeek distilled model 可能需要不同的 fine-tuning recipe (更高 rank, 更多 epoch, 不同 lr)。\"\n\n  - name: \"deepseek-cls-repo-s123\"\n    plan_id: \"repo-level-training\"\n    description: \"DeepSeek repo-level CLS seed 123 for multi-seed variance estimation.\"\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 72.3\n      f1_macro: 61.8\n      f1_fail: 43.6\n      f1_pass: 80.0\n      majority_baseline: 72.96\n      gap_vs_majority_pp: -0.66\n      unparseable_pct: 2.1\n      best_checkpoint: \"checkpoint-400\"\n    result_rationale: \"Seed variance 在小数据 repo-level 上极大。N_test=48 (instance-level) 或 ~9784 (per-test) 但 effective N 受 block correlation 限制 (~48 independent units)。Seed 123 恰好比 seed 42 差 2.5pp — 这在 48 个 instance 上是 1-2 个 instance 的差异。accuracy 72.3% 甚至低于 majority baseline，证明 seed variance 使结果不可靠。两个 seed 的 spread 为 2.5pp，预示需要 5+ seeds 才能得到有意义的 CI。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"CLS seed variance: 72.3% - 74.8% (2.5pp spread with just 2 seeds)。CI 包含 majority baseline，无法声称 CLS significantly better than chance at repo-level for DeepSeek。\"\n\n  - name: \"deepseek-cwm-repo\"\n    plan_id: \"repo-level-training\"\n    description: \"DeepSeek repo-level CWM generation, seed 42, 8k seq, max_new_tokens=512.\"\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 70.2\n      f1_macro: 55.8\n      f1_pass: 78.9\n      f1_fail: 32.7\n      unparseable_pct: 28.5\n      unparseable_count: 2789\n      exact_match_rate: 18.3\n      majority_baseline: 72.96\n      gap_vs_majority_pp: -2.76\n      parseable_only_accuracy: 76.4\n      best_checkpoint: \"checkpoint-400\"\n      total_samples: 9784\n      gen_length_mean: 4200\n      gen_length_median: 3800\n    result_rationale: \"DeepSeek 在 func-level CWM 有 0% unparseable (tokenizer 支持结构化输出)，但 repo-level 的输出格式更复杂 (多 test 结果拼接)，unparseable 上升到 28.5%。这比 Qwen 的 93% 好得多，但仍然不 trivial。关键 confound: 70.2% accuracy 低于 majority baseline，意味着模型在学到 format 的 subset 上仍然 discriminate 得不好。Parseable-only accuracy 76.4% 略高于 baseline 但 F1-fail 极低 (32.7%)，模型严重偏向预测 pass。DeepSeek CWM unparseable_pct=28.5% 处于 worst-case 范围 [5, 60] 的中间，足以使结果 ambiguous: 不像 Qwen (93%) 那样可以明确归因于 tokenizer failure，也不像 0% 那样可以 fairly compare。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: DeepSeek Repo CWM vs CLS\"\n        columns: [\"Formulation\", \"Accuracy\", \"Unparseable%\", \"F1-macro\", \"Δ vs Majority\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"CLS (s42)\", \"74.8%\", \"1.8%\", \"65.2\", \"+1.84pp\"]\n          - [\"CWM (s42)\", \"70.2%\", \"28.5%\", \"55.8\", \"-2.76pp\"]\n          - [\"Gap (CLS-CWM)\", \"+4.6pp\", \"—\", \"+9.4\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Comparison showing both CLS and CWM hovering near majority baseline, with large error bars from seed variance.\"\n    analysis: \"CLS-CWM gap = +4.6pp，在 worst-case 范围 [-5, 5] 的边界附近。但两者都接近/低于 majority baseline，使 gap 的实际意义存疑。无法判断: 是 CLS genuinely better at repo-level (支持 Qwen narrative)，还是两者都 fail 只是 fail 的方式不同。28.5% unparseable 是 'middle ground' confound — 不够高以明确归因 tokenizer，不够低以 fairly compare accuracy。\"\n\n  - name: \"deepseek-cwm-repo-s123\"\n    plan_id: \"repo-level-training\"\n    description: \"DeepSeek repo-level CWM seed 123.\"\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 68.5\n      f1_macro: 52.1\n      f1_fail: 28.9\n      f1_pass: 75.3\n      unparseable_pct: 35.2\n      majority_baseline: 72.96\n      gap_vs_majority_pp: -4.46\n      best_checkpoint: \"checkpoint-600\"\n    result_rationale: \"Seed 123 的 CWM 表现更差: unparseable 上升到 35.2% (生成长度 distribution shift)，accuracy 进一步低于 baseline。两个 CWM seeds 的 spread = 1.7pp accuracy，但 unparseable spread = 6.7pp，说明生成质量高度不稳定。CLS-CWM gap 在此 seed = 72.3 - 68.5 = 3.8pp，与 seed42 的 4.6pp 方向一致但 magnitude 不同。问题: 在两者都低于 majority baseline 时，'CLS > CWM' 的声称有什么意义？\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Cross-seed CWM: 68.5-70.2% (1.7pp spread)。Cross-seed CLS: 72.3-74.8% (2.5pp)。Gap 范围 3.8-4.6pp。但 combined CI (bootstrap over seeds + instances) 会包含 0，无法达到统计显著。\"\n\n  - name: \"deepseek-repo-combined-analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"repo-level-training\"\n    description: \"Combined analysis across DeepSeek repo-level experiments: CLS vs CWM with multi-seed bootstrap CI.\"\n    expected_results:\n      cls_mean_accuracy: 73.55\n      cls_std_accuracy: 1.77\n      cwm_mean_accuracy: 69.35\n      cwm_std_accuracy: 1.2\n      cls_cwm_gap_mean_pp: 4.2\n      cls_cwm_gap_95CI: [-1.8, 10.2]\n      paired_t_test_p: 0.18\n      majority_baseline: 72.96\n      cls_vs_majority_p: 0.71\n      cwm_vs_majority_p: 0.12\n      n_seeds: 2\n      effective_n_instances: 48\n      power_at_5pp_effect: 0.31\n    result_rationale: \"只有 2 seeds × 48 effective instances，statistical power 极低 (0.31 for 5pp effect)。即使真实 effect 存在，也 underpowered to detect。CI [-1.8, 10.2] 包含 0，无法拒绝 H0。更致命的是 CLS 本身相对 majority baseline 不显著 (p=0.71)，说明 DeepSeek 在 repo-level 整体 fine-tuning 失败。这不是 formulation 问题而是 model/recipe 问题，使 CLS vs CWM 比较 confounded by underlying training failure。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: DeepSeek Repo-level Summary (Worst-case)\"\n        columns: [\"\", \"CLS\", \"CWM\", \"TRAJ (8k)\", \"Majority\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Seed 42\", \"74.8%\", \"70.2%\", \"81.25%\", \"73.0%\"]\n          - [\"Seed 123\", \"72.3%\", \"68.5%\", \"75.0%\", \"73.0%\"]\n          - [\"Mean\", \"73.6%\", \"69.4%\", \"78.1% (6seeds: 75.4±5.1)\", \"73.0%\"]\n          - [\"vs Majority\", \"+0.6pp\", \"-3.6pp\", \"+5.1pp\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Box plot showing DeepSeek repo-level results: all formulations cluster near majority baseline with massive seed variance, TRAJ slightly above but with enormous spread.\"\n    analysis: \"Confound 明确: (1) CLS 不 work (≈majority)，所以 CLS > CWM 的 claim 无法从 'CLS better' 推断，只能说 'CWM worse than chance'; (2) TRAJ 是唯一 reliably above majority 的 formulation (6 seeds mean 75.4%)，但 seed variance 5.1pp 极大; (3) 无法得出 directional conclusion 关于 formulation ranking at repo-level for DeepSeek。只能 scope down: 'DeepSeek repo-level 在当前 LoRA recipe 下 underfits，需要 larger-scale study with different hyperparameters'。\"\n\n  - name: \"swebench-pertest-data\"\n    plan_id: \"swebench-pertest-data\"\n    description: \"Docker re-evaluation of SWE-bench Verified patches, per-test label extraction. CPU-only.\"\n    expected_results:\n      n_instances_attempted: 500\n      n_instances_successful: 423\n      n_instances_docker_fail: 77\n      n_candidates_per_instance: 16\n      total_per_test_labels: 87000\n      docker_timeout_pct: 8.2\n      median_tests_per_instance: 12\n      mean_tests_per_instance: 18.4\n      f2p_test_count_distribution:\n        T1: 0.45\n        T2: 0.22\n        T3_5: 0.18\n        T6plus: 0.15\n    result_rationale: \"数据构建本身不受 worst tier 影响 — 这是 infrastructure work。423/500 成功率合理 (SWE-bench docker environments 有一定比例 flaky/timeout)。数据集本身会如预期构建完成。问题不在数据而在下游使用: 即使数据 ready，在 worst tier 下 repo-level training 和 re-repair 都不 work，数据集的 practical value 仅限于 'resource contribution'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"数据集构建预期成功。但 worst tier 下其下游 experiments 全部 null/confounded，削弱了数据集作为 contribution 的 narrative (需要 show 有人能用它做出有意义的结果)。\"\n\n  - name: \"qwen-repo-error-complementarity\"\n    plan_id: \"repo-level-training\"\n    description: \"Error complementarity analysis between CLS and CWM at repo-level (Qwen), analogous to function-level oracle ensemble.\"\n    expected_results:\n      cls_accuracy: 82.35\n      cwm_accuracy_parseable_only: 42.9\n      cwm_parseable_rate: 46.3\n      oracle_ensemble_accuracy_parseable_subset: 51.2\n      oracle_ensemble_full_set: null\n      complementarity_ratio: null\n    result_rationale: \"Qwen repo-level CWM 有 93% unparseable，使 complementarity analysis 无法执行 — 只有 7% 的 samples 有 CWM predictions。在可解析的 subset 上 CWM accuracy 仅 42.9%，低于 random。Oracle ensemble 在这个 tiny subset 上无统计意义。无法复现 function-level 的 error complementarity story (90.63% oracle) at repo-level。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Error complementarity 只在 function-level 成立 (两个 formulation 都 work 时)。Repo-level 由于 CWM collapse 无法做此分析。这进一步限制了 paper 能讲的 story。\"\n```\n\n**总结**: Worst tier 的核心灾难是三重的:\n1. **Re-repair 完全 null** — B vs A1 仅 +1.7pp (CI 含 0)，B vs D 仅 +0.7pp (CLS-specific signal = 0)\n2. **DeepSeek repo CLS 本身不 work** — 仅 +0.6pp vs majority，使 CLS vs CWM 比较 meaningless\n3. **Seed variance + small N** — 所有 repo-level 结论 underpowered (power=0.31)\n\n叙事策略: 完全砍掉 re-repair section + 将 DeepSeek repo 降级为 \"preliminary case study showing need for larger-scale investigation\"。Paper 核心只剩 function-level equivalence + efficiency + Qwen repo-level tokenizer finding。"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":33642,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":33642},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b649b12d-6842-4938-9e21-936da6c17cfc","uuid":"c1b9ea40-a302-4687-8330-a05730f33010"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":150352,"duration_api_ms":152365,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: \"完全放弃 re-repair section，不放入论文。Reframe: (1) efficiency 6-9x speedup 作为核心 practical contribution; (2) 强化 error complementarity (oracle 90.63%) 作为 formulations are complementary 的证据; (3) DeepSeek repo scope down 为 case study 而非 systematic comparison。仍投 EMNLP Main，但 novelty argument 必须极其清晰。Fallback: ICSE 2027。\"\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"re-repair-phase1-instruct\"\n    plan_id: \"diagnostic-rerepair\"\n    description: \"Re-repair with Qwen3-8B-Instruct on 60 SWE-bench instances, 5 conditions (A1-minimal, A2-test-names, B-CLS-diagnostic, C-oracle, D-random), pass@1/pass@5, Docker eval, paired design.\"\n    expected_results:\n      n_instances: 60\n      n_conditions: 5\n      samples_per_condition: 5\n      A1_minimal_resolve_rate_pass1: 0.183\n      A2_test_names_resolve_rate_pass1: 0.200\n      B_cls_diagnostic_resolve_rate_pass1: 0.200\n      C_oracle_diagnostic_resolve_rate_pass1: 0.217\n      D_random_diagnostic_resolve_rate_pass1: 0.193\n      A1_resolve_rate_pass5: 0.317\n      B_resolve_rate_pass5: 0.333\n      C_resolve_rate_pass5: 0.367\n      D_resolve_rate_pass5: 0.317\n      delta_B_vs_A1_pp: 1.7\n      delta_C_vs_A1_pp: 3.4\n      delta_D_vs_A1_pp: 1.0\n      delta_B_vs_D_pp: 0.7\n      delta_C_vs_B_pp: 1.7\n      paired_mcnemar_B_vs_A1_p: 0.72\n      paired_mcnemar_B_vs_D_p: 0.83\n      CI_95_B_vs_A1: [-4.2, 7.5]\n      prompt_format1_delta_B_A1: 2.3\n      prompt_format2_delta_B_A1: 1.0\n    result_rationale: \"Repair agent (Qwen3-8B-Instruct) 本身 resolve rate ~18% — 在此低基线下 per-test diagnostic 的信息增益被 agent 的代码理解能力瓶颈淹没。Agent 在多数情况下无法利用 'test_X fails with expected Y got Z' 信息来定位 bug，因为 bug 本身需要 repo-level 理解。Oracle (C) 仅略好于 CLS (B) 证明即使 diagnostic 完美准确也帮助有限。Random (D) 与 B 无显著差异，说明 agent 对任何额外 context 的反应类似 — 可能只是 prompt 长度/结构的 placebo effect 而非 CLS-specific signal。60 instances × 5 samples 的 power 不足以检测 <5pp 的差异 (所需 n≈200+)。复现 phase0 的 null pattern: 所有带 diagnostic 的 condition 都与 control 无统计显著差异。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Re-repair Resolve Rate by Condition\"\n        columns: [\"Condition\", \"pass@1\", \"pass@5\", \"Δ vs A1 (pp)\", \"p-value\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"A1 (minimal)\", \"18.3%\", \"31.7%\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"A2 (test-names)\", \"20.0%\", \"30.0%\", \"+1.7\", \"0.81\"]\n          - [\"B (CLS-diag)\", \"20.0%\", \"33.3%\", \"+1.7\", \"0.72\"]\n          - [\"C (Oracle-diag)\", \"21.7%\", \"36.7%\", \"+3.4\", \"0.48\"]\n          - [\"D (Random-diag)\", \"19.3%\", \"31.7%\", \"+1.0\", \"0.89\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart showing resolve rate across 5 conditions with 95% CI error bars; all CIs heavily overlap, visually indistinguishable.\"\n    analysis: \"完全 null result。B vs A1 的 1.7pp 差异远在 noise 范围内 (CI: -4.2 to +7.5)。B vs D 差异 0.7pp 证明 CLS-specific information 没有比 random noise 更好。即使 oracle (C) 也仅 +3.4pp，表明 per-test failure localization 本身对当前 repair agent 无用。结论: diagnostic info 不改变 repair agent 行为。此 section 如放入论文只会暴露 'no downstream utility' 弱点，应完全删除。\"\n\n  - name: \"deepseek-cls-repo-v4\"\n    plan_id: \"repo-level-training\"\n    description: \"DeepSeek-R1-0528-Qwen3-8B LoRA classification at repo-level, seed 42, 8k seq length, same SWE-bench-PerTest data as Qwen experiments.\"\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 74.8\n      f1_macro: 65.2\n      f1_pass: 82.1\n      f1_fail: 48.3\n      precision_fail: 55.7\n      recall_fail: 42.8\n      precision_pass: 79.6\n      recall_pass: 84.7\n      majority_baseline: 72.96\n      gap_vs_majority_pp: 1.84\n      unparseable_pct: 1.8\n      train_loss_final: 0.42\n      eval_loss_best: 0.38\n      best_checkpoint: \"checkpoint-400\"\n      total_samples: 9784\n      overfitting_detected: true\n    result_rationale: \"DeepSeek 8B (distilled from R1) 在 repo-level 上表现远不如 function-level (func: 86.9%)。原因: (1) repo-level 输入平均 6-8k tokens，DeepSeek 的 LoRA rank=16 容量不足以学会长上下文中的 pass/fail 信号; (2) 训练数据仅 ~3k repo-level instances (vs func-level 9.5k)，data-starved; (3) 74.8% 仅高于 majority baseline 1.84pp，实质上模型主要学到了 class prior 而非 discriminative features。与 Qwen 8B 在同数据上的 84.79% (ckpt-400) 相比低 10pp，表明 DeepSeek distilled model 的 LoRA fine-tuning effectiveness 显著低于 Qwen — 这是 confound: 我们无法区分 'formulation difference' 和 'model fine-tuning efficiency difference'。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: DeepSeek Repo-level CLS Performance\"\n        columns: [\"Checkpoint\", \"Accuracy\", \"F1-macro\", \"Fail-F1\", \"Gap vs Majority\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"ckpt-200\", \"71.2%\", \"58.3\", \"38.7\", \"-1.76pp\"]\n          - [\"ckpt-400\", \"74.8%\", \"65.2\", \"48.3\", \"+1.84pp\"]\n          - [\"ckpt-600\", \"73.1%\", \"62.8\", \"44.1\", \"+0.14pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Learning curve showing rapid overfitting after step 400, eval loss climbing while train loss drops.\"\n    analysis: \"CLS 在 DeepSeek repo-level 仅比 majority baseline 高 ~2pp，远低于 Qwen 8B 的 +12pp gap。这使 cross-model comparison 失去意义: 如果 CLS 本身不 work，CLS vs CWM 的比较没有 informative value。Confound: DeepSeek distilled model 可能需要不同的 fine-tuning recipe (更高 rank, 更多 epoch, 不同 lr)。\"\n\n  - name: \"deepseek-cls-repo-s123\"\n    plan_id: \"repo-level-training\"\n    description: \"DeepSeek repo-level CLS seed 123 for multi-seed variance estimation.\"\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 72.3\n      f1_macro: 61.8\n      f1_fail: 43.6\n      f1_pass: 80.0\n      majority_baseline: 72.96\n      gap_vs_majority_pp: -0.66\n      unparseable_pct: 2.1\n      best_checkpoint: \"checkpoint-400\"\n    result_rationale: \"Seed variance 在小数据 repo-level 上极大。N_test=48 (instance-level) 或 ~9784 (per-test) 但 effective N 受 block correlation 限制 (~48 independent units)。Seed 123 恰好比 seed 42 差 2.5pp — 这在 48 个 instance 上是 1-2 个 instance 的差异。accuracy 72.3% 甚至低于 majority baseline，证明 seed variance 使结果不可靠。两个 seed 的 spread 为 2.5pp，预示需要 5+ seeds 才能得到有意义的 CI。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"CLS seed variance: 72.3% - 74.8% (2.5pp spread with just 2 seeds)。CI 包含 majority baseline，无法声称 CLS significantly better than chance at repo-level for DeepSeek。\"\n\n  - name: \"deepseek-cwm-repo\"\n    plan_id: \"repo-level-training\"\n    description: \"DeepSeek repo-level CWM generation, seed 42, 8k seq, max_new_tokens=512.\"\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 70.2\n      f1_macro: 55.8\n      f1_pass: 78.9\n      f1_fail: 32.7\n      unparseable_pct: 28.5\n      unparseable_count: 2789\n      exact_match_rate: 18.3\n      majority_baseline: 72.96\n      gap_vs_majority_pp: -2.76\n      parseable_only_accuracy: 76.4\n      best_checkpoint: \"checkpoint-400\"\n      total_samples: 9784\n      gen_length_mean: 4200\n      gen_length_median: 3800\n    result_rationale: \"DeepSeek 在 func-level CWM 有 0% unparseable (tokenizer 支持结构化输出)，但 repo-level 的输出格式更复杂 (多 test 结果拼接)，unparseable 上升到 28.5%。这比 Qwen 的 93% 好得多，但仍然不 trivial。关键 confound: 70.2% accuracy 低于 majority baseline，意味着模型在学到 format 的 subset 上仍然 discriminate 得不好。Parseable-only accuracy 76.4% 略高于 baseline 但 F1-fail 极低 (32.7%)，模型严重偏向预测 pass。DeepSeek CWM unparseable_pct=28.5% 处于 worst-case 范围 [5, 60] 的中间，足以使结果 ambiguous: 不像 Qwen (93%) 那样可以明确归因于 tokenizer failure，也不像 0% 那样可以 fairly compare。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: DeepSeek Repo CWM vs CLS\"\n        columns: [\"Formulation\", \"Accuracy\", \"Unparseable%\", \"F1-macro\", \"Δ vs Majority\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"CLS (s42)\", \"74.8%\", \"1.8%\", \"65.2\", \"+1.84pp\"]\n          - [\"CWM (s42)\", \"70.2%\", \"28.5%\", \"55.8\", \"-2.76pp\"]\n          - [\"Gap (CLS-CWM)\", \"+4.6pp\", \"—\", \"+9.4\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Comparison showing both CLS and CWM hovering near majority baseline, with large error bars from seed variance.\"\n    analysis: \"CLS-CWM gap = +4.6pp，在 worst-case 范围 [-5, 5] 的边界附近。但两者都接近/低于 majority baseline，使 gap 的实际意义存疑。无法判断: 是 CLS genuinely better at repo-level (支持 Qwen narrative)，还是两者都 fail 只是 fail 的方式不同。28.5% unparseable 是 'middle ground' confound — 不够高以明确归因 tokenizer，不够低以 fairly compare accuracy。\"\n\n  - name: \"deepseek-cwm-repo-s123\"\n    plan_id: \"repo-level-training\"\n    description: \"DeepSeek repo-level CWM seed 123.\"\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 68.5\n      f1_macro: 52.1\n      f1_fail: 28.9\n      f1_pass: 75.3\n      unparseable_pct: 35.2\n      majority_baseline: 72.96\n      gap_vs_majority_pp: -4.46\n      best_checkpoint: \"checkpoint-600\"\n    result_rationale: \"Seed 123 的 CWM 表现更差: unparseable 上升到 35.2% (生成长度 distribution shift)，accuracy 进一步低于 baseline。两个 CWM seeds 的 spread = 1.7pp accuracy，但 unparseable spread = 6.7pp，说明生成质量高度不稳定。CLS-CWM gap 在此 seed = 72.3 - 68.5 = 3.8pp，与 seed42 的 4.6pp 方向一致但 magnitude 不同。问题: 在两者都低于 majority baseline 时，'CLS > CWM' 的声称有什么意义？\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Cross-seed CWM: 68.5-70.2% (1.7pp spread)。Cross-seed CLS: 72.3-74.8% (2.5pp)。Gap 范围 3.8-4.6pp。但 combined CI (bootstrap over seeds + instances) 会包含 0，无法达到统计显著。\"\n\n  - name: \"deepseek-repo-combined-analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"repo-level-training\"\n    description: \"Combined analysis across DeepSeek repo-level experiments: CLS vs CWM with multi-seed bootstrap CI.\"\n    expected_results:\n      cls_mean_accuracy: 73.55\n      cls_std_accuracy: 1.77\n      cwm_mean_accuracy: 69.35\n      cwm_std_accuracy: 1.2\n      cls_cwm_gap_mean_pp: 4.2\n      cls_cwm_gap_95CI: [-1.8, 10.2]\n      paired_t_test_p: 0.18\n      majority_baseline: 72.96\n      cls_vs_majority_p: 0.71\n      cwm_vs_majority_p: 0.12\n      n_seeds: 2\n      effective_n_instances: 48\n      power_at_5pp_effect: 0.31\n    result_rationale: \"只有 2 seeds × 48 effective instances，statistical power 极低 (0.31 for 5pp effect)。即使真实 effect 存在，也 underpowered to detect。CI [-1.8, 10.2] 包含 0，无法拒绝 H0。更致命的是 CLS 本身相对 majority baseline 不显著 (p=0.71)，说明 DeepSeek 在 repo-level 整体 fine-tuning 失败。这不是 formulation 问题而是 model/recipe 问题，使 CLS vs CWM 比较 confounded by underlying training failure。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: DeepSeek Repo-level Summary (Worst-case)\"\n        columns: [\"\", \"CLS\", \"CWM\", \"TRAJ (8k)\", \"Majority\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Seed 42\", \"74.8%\", \"70.2%\", \"81.25%\", \"73.0%\"]\n          - [\"Seed 123\", \"72.3%\", \"68.5%\", \"75.0%\", \"73.0%\"]\n          - [\"Mean\", \"73.6%\", \"69.4%\", \"78.1% (6seeds: 75.4±5.1)\", \"73.0%\"]\n          - [\"vs Majority\", \"+0.6pp\", \"-3.6pp\", \"+5.1pp\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Box plot showing DeepSeek repo-level results: all formulations cluster near majority baseline with massive seed variance, TRAJ slightly above but with enormous spread.\"\n    analysis: \"Confound 明确: (1) CLS 不 work (≈majority)，所以 CLS > CWM 的 claim 无法从 'CLS better' 推断，只能说 'CWM worse than chance'; (2) TRAJ 是唯一 reliably above majority 的 formulation (6 seeds mean 75.4%)，但 seed variance 5.1pp 极大; (3) 无法得出 directional conclusion 关于 formulation ranking at repo-level for DeepSeek。只能 scope down: 'DeepSeek repo-level 在当前 LoRA recipe 下 underfits，需要 larger-scale study with different hyperparameters'。\"\n\n  - name: \"swebench-pertest-data\"\n    plan_id: \"swebench-pertest-data\"\n    description: \"Docker re-evaluation of SWE-bench Verified patches, per-test label extraction. CPU-only.\"\n    expected_results:\n      n_instances_attempted: 500\n      n_instances_successful: 423\n      n_instances_docker_fail: 77\n      n_candidates_per_instance: 16\n      total_per_test_labels: 87000\n      docker_timeout_pct: 8.2\n      median_tests_per_instance: 12\n      mean_tests_per_instance: 18.4\n      f2p_test_count_distribution:\n        T1: 0.45\n        T2: 0.22\n        T3_5: 0.18\n        T6plus: 0.15\n    result_rationale: \"数据构建本身不受 worst tier 影响 — 这是 infrastructure work。423/500 成功率合理 (SWE-bench docker environments 有一定比例 flaky/timeout)。数据集本身会如预期构建完成。问题不在数据而在下游使用: 即使数据 ready，在 worst tier 下 repo-level training 和 re-repair 都不 work，数据集的 practical value 仅限于 'resource contribution'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"数据集构建预期成功。但 worst tier 下其下游 experiments 全部 null/confounded，削弱了数据集作为 contribution 的 narrative (需要 show 有人能用它做出有意义的结果)。\"\n\n  - name: \"qwen-repo-error-complementarity\"\n    plan_id: \"repo-level-training\"\n    description: \"Error complementarity analysis between CLS and CWM at repo-level (Qwen), analogous to function-level oracle ensemble.\"\n    expected_results:\n      cls_accuracy: 82.35\n      cwm_accuracy_parseable_only: 42.9\n      cwm_parseable_rate: 46.3\n      oracle_ensemble_accuracy_parseable_subset: 51.2\n      oracle_ensemble_full_set: null\n      complementarity_ratio: null\n    result_rationale: \"Qwen repo-level CWM 有 93% unparseable，使 complementarity analysis 无法执行 — 只有 7% 的 samples 有 CWM predictions。在可解析的 subset 上 CWM accuracy 仅 42.9%，低于 random。Oracle ensemble 在这个 tiny subset 上无统计意义。无法复现 function-level 的 error complementarity story (90.63% oracle) at repo-level。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Error complementarity 只在 function-level 成立 (两个 formulation 都 work 时)。Repo-level 由于 CWM collapse 无法做此分析。这进一步限制了 paper 能讲的 story。\"\n```\n\n**总结**: Worst tier 的核心灾难是三重的:\n1. **Re-repair 完全 null** — B vs A1 仅 +1.7pp (CI 含 0)，B vs D 仅 +0.7pp (CLS-specific signal = 0)\n2. **DeepSeek repo CLS 本身不 work** — 仅 +0.6pp vs majority，使 CLS vs CWM 比较 meaningless\n3. **Seed variance + small N** — 所有 repo-level 结论 underpowered (power=0.31)\n\n叙事策略: 完全砍掉 re-repair section + 将 DeepSeek repo 降级为 \"preliminary case study showing need for larger-scale investigation\"。Paper 核心只剩 function-level equivalence + efficiency + Qwen repo-level tokenizer finding。","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"b649b12d-6842-4938-9e21-936da6c17cfc","total_cost_usd":0.420425,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":33642,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"output_tokens":7045,"